WEBVTT

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.000
The candidates to enter the
musical department have been decided

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.700
and we, the Kao Council, have also
chosen the students for the Star Teams, but--

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.040
"Kakeru Tengenji | Toru Nayuki | Yuta Hoshitani"

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.040
But, you know--

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.040
Huh? Is there a problem?

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.790
They have not even met the
criteria to pass the entrance audition.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.910
You would pick five students like
that and put them on a Star Team?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.950
I have my own passing criteria, though.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:04.660
Otori, don't get carried away just because
you've managed to sneak onto the Kao Council.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:05.750
You probably just got
in because of the chairman--

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.910
Akatsuki.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.000
Sorry, Hiragi.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.040
I cannot think you made
those choices in your right mind.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.700
I'm always in my right mind.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.950
<i>Très bien</i> ! As expected of our class rebel.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Do what you want.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.500
Hiragi!

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.250
Everyone on the Kao Council is equal.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:42.450
Otori, you can choose whomever you want
as long as you take responsibility for them.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.120
Then, I'll take you at your word.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.370
The ones who will aim for the future
as the newly formed Team Otori are...

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:51.000
...these five!

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:54.370
"Kakeru Tengenji | Toru Nayuki | Yuta Hoshitani
| Shu Kuga | Kaito Tsukigami"

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.500
He's in the musical department, right?

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.410
On top of that, he's on a Star Team!

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.000
Musical department Star Team...

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.000
"Here!!" "Practice Room"

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.000
Team Otori's first practice!

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.620
Huh?!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.120
This is where the practice room is?

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.830
Excuse me!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.540
Huh?

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.910
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:52.250
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:59.410
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:07.250
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.750
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:15.290
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:23.540
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:29.790
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.830
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:38.290
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:42.040
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:47.790
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:52.250
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.450
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.000
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.500
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.250
"Act 2"

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.250
Oh, Hoshitani.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.160
Nayuki!

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.200
I'm Yuta Hoshitani!

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.330
I look forward to working
with you from now on!

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.290
Why are <i>you</i> here?

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.500
Why?

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.250
You don't think it's strange, you amateur?

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.040
What do you mean?

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.370
Oh, you're in a different class,
so you wouldn't know.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:39.290
This guy came from a regular school
that didn't even have a music course.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:41.750
That's why he came so late.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.040
But I came when we were told to.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.790
That's when we <i>start</i> practice.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:54.250
In other words, you should already
be done warming up by then, you boor.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.620
T-Tengenji...

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.450
I'm in the same team as someone like <i>this</i> ?

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.700
Hmph, it must be a mistake.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:08.290
We can find out if it was a mistake
or not by asking the one who chose us.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.370
Who would that be?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.290
If I remember correctly,
his name is Itsuki Otori.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:29.160
♪ Stretch out your hand as far as it'll go ♪

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:37.120
♪ Tempted by the passionate
dream so hot it practically burns ♪

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.330
♪ The curtain goes up on the show ♪

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:45.250
♪ Right now I'm flyin' high
in the center of the light! ♪

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:50.620
♪ It'll be a miracle! ♪

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.290
♪ If there's something you want ♪

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.290
♪ Then yell out that you want it ♪

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:15.200
♪ Words will bring magic ♪

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.000
♪ Don't walk, run ♪

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.830
♪ Don't run, dance ♪

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:27.000
♪ Chasing your dreams ♪

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.200
♪ The best... (That's...) ♪

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.160
♪ ...star max! (...star max) ♪

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:42.450
♪ Watch from where you are, and I'll prove it ♪

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.750
♪ Open your arms and embrace ♪

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:55.700
♪ These cheers and the
swirl of unending applause ♪

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.330
♪ Don't just love, be loved! ♪

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:03.660
♪ You have been chosen by God ♪

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:08.830
♪ Flyin' fire bird! ♪

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.000
Welcome to Team Otori!

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.620
For the rest of this year--

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.620
Wait a minute!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.700
Isn't there someone who got in by mistake?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.910
Huh? You mean, <i>you</i> ?

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.830
Just kidding.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.950
All five of you here are
part of the Star Team I chose.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.660
There's no mistake.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:39.290
Now, since we're all here,
why don't you introduce yourselves?

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.700
Starting with you.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.120
Uh, yes, sir!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.040
I am Yuta Hoshitani.
I look forward to working with everyone.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.870
I am Toru Nayuki.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.660
Kaito Tsukigami. Nice to meet you.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.370
Shu Kuga.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.870
I'm Kakeru Tengenji.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.450
Okay, you guys are a team starting from today.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:05.000
In order to survive this year, the five
of you have to cooperate and work hard.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.790
Survive?

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.790
Just because you were
selected in these auditions

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:12.370
doesn't mean you're in the musical department.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.330
Huh? It doesn't?

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:17.120
Because the musical department
is a specialized course,

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.450
you will officially enter in your second year.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:24.450
In other words, as first years,
you are just candidates.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:29.700
The twenty teams, including the
five Star Teams, that were selected

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.700
have only made it past the
first round of the screening process.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:37.290
After the second round that is
the Newcomers' Debut Performance,

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.950
half of those--ten teams--will be eliminated.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.950
The final selection will take
place on stage at the Ayanagi Festival,

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:47.370
where another half of
the teams will be eliminated.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:54.500
Only five teams--25 people--will be
officially admitted to the music department.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:57.330
Only 25 people...

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.040
Also, this should be obvious,

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.330
but just because you are on a Star Team
doesn't mean you get special treatment.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:08.540
The only perk you have is that
you can learn from us, the Kao Council.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:12.000
But isn't that a pretty big advantage?

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.700
That depends on you all.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.290
Well, why don't we get started?

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:22.950
Now, boys! It's time to play!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.330
"Ayanagi Academy Murder Case"
"Act 4"

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.540
I'll have you put this on today.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.910
"Ayanagi Academy Murder Case"?

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.540
That script contains the climax of the story.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.290
The principal of Ayanagi
Academy has been killed,

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:40.290
and a detective has gathered the
four suspects, the four sons of the principal,

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:43.700
and is in pursuit of the culprit.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:47.290
I'll assign your parts.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.700
Tsukigami will play the serious oldest son.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:53.040
He's fighting with their father
about how to run the school.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.790
Okay.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:57.330
Kuga will play the silent second son.

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:02.290
He's unhappy with their father
because of their dead mother.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.200
Tengenji will play the prodigal third son.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.370
He was almost disinherited by their father.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.660
Nayuki will play the shy fourth son.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.330
He always wanted their
father to acknowledge him.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:15.620
Yes, sir!

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:18.910
And the detective chasing after
them will be played by Hoshitani.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.120
I-I'll be the detective?

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.910
Yeah. Now, get ready.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.200
The detective is the main character, right?

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.040
I wonder if this means
he has high hopes for me.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.080
It's easy to prepare for the role of detective
since what he needs to do is obvious.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:38.330
It's the perfect part for an amateur.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:41.200
Oh, I'm so nervous...

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.410
Now, shall we begin?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.580
W-Without even a read-through?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.080
It'll be easier to figure out
your abilities that way.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:59.700
Ayanagi Academy Murder Case, start!

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.830
Wasn't Father's death ruled an accident--?

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.370
I don't have time for this!

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:09.160
What did you gather us here for?

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:11.410
I know who the culprit is.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.830
The culprit is...

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.410
...one of <i>you</i> !

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:20.660
That was perfect.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.000
It's hard to play off that.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.450
Hoshitani...

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.790
He's overacting.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.620
Th-That's cruel.
There's no way we would kill Father.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:34.540
Say it straight! Who's the culprit?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.700
You have proof, right?

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.540
Of course I have proof.

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:40.540
Then who are you saying did it?

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:43.910
Who is it? Please tell us, Detective.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.500
Very well. The culprit is--

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.910
U-Um, this is...

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.250
Continue!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.040
The curtain is still up.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.160
Don't tell me we're doing improv from day one?

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:17.830
You're quick to understand.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:19.290
Seriously?

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.790
Um... What's "improv"?

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.000
You don't even know <i>that</i> ?

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.950
"Improv" is short for improvisation.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.870
Does that mean...?

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:29.790
That's right.

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:32.660
I'm leaving the rest of this to you all.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:36.000
I would like you to bring
this story to a proper ending.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.660
Th-That's impossible...
I mean, even Hoshitani's...

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.080
All right!

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.450
He's totally confident?!

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.790
Okay, places!

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:49.950
Start from the oldest brother's line at
the end of the fourth page and keep going.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:04.450
Now, boys! Let's have fun with this!

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:08.540
Who is it? Please tell us, Detective.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:12.120
Very well. The culprit is--

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:18.080
The culprit is... The culprit is...

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:21.120
Um... The culprit is...

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.870
Don't tell me, this guy...

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.870
Hoshitani...

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.580
...has no plan?!

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:29.000
Um... The culprit is... is...

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.040
If he says it's me with
no plan in mind, it'll be hell!

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.950
Wherever he steers us now could
make all our hard work go to waste!

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.330
I think...

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.370
...the culprit is...

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:41.870
Detective, please stop!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.540
Huh?

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:50.410
Who killed Father...?

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:53.370
I don't want to know!

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:55.580
He's pretty good for an ordinary person.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:59.040
But does he have a proper resolution in mind?

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.450
Nayuki's amazing!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.330
I have to keep going, too!

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.790
But how should I answer...?

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:07.410
Please wait!

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:11.660
I would like you to tell us how you can
even call it a murder in the first place!

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.500
He changed the flow, huh?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:16.200
As expected of a thoroughbred
from the musical world.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.950
But I won't let you be
the only one to look good.

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:24.410
That's right, you said earlier
that you had proof, didn't you?

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:27.660
There's a reason he's called the
"young noble of the <i>kabuki</i> world," huh?

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.370
That connected well.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:35.000
Amazing. Tsukigami and Tengenji
both sound like they have scripts.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.120
But even I can...

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.790
Th-The proof is...!

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.790
We're back where we started?

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:41.950
Who's left?

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.830
That guy hasn't done anything yet!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.500
Is he really planning on letting
it continue without doing anything?

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.290
Be of some use, you blockhead!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.040
Why are you always like that?

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.540
Pretending that you don't see
anything that's going on within the family!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:10.750
Don't you have a shred
of feeling for this family?!

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.870
Your brothers are under suspicion, and you--

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.540
Please wait! This is the proof!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:25.080
This is what your father
left with his last strength...

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.540
...his dying message!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:36.750
The name of the culprit is written here.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.370
And it is...

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:42.120
Second son! It's you!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.040
P-Poison?!

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:03.950
Idiot! Killing your father
won't make your mother happy!

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:07.830
Bastard, when did he prepare the fake blood?

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.410
But where did he get that dying message?

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.950
Don't you die, too!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.200
Don't die!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.410
Okay, stop!

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:22.620
Well, that was pretty good for your first time.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.540
So, that's enough for today.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:44.120
Um, Kuga, was it? Thanks for this.

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:50.370
Giving him a note like that won't
help him in the long run, you know.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.700
Sorry, I took some.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.750
Sure.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.040
Everyone's amazing!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:08.330
Jeez, what're you so happy about?
This was like a school play, you amateur.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.250
Amateur...

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.250
It's understandable that he'd call me that.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.410
Everyone had to keep helping me.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:16.790
It's not like I was helping you.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.620
I just performed until the end.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:31.450
You could at least tell me what you thought.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.790
What are you talking about?

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.660
You should be more honest.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.660
It was pretty interesting, wasn't it?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.000
Interesting?

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:44.830
It's problematic if the limited
Star Team spots were filled for that reason.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.830
Let me put it bluntly.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:49.410
I do not approve of the way you do things.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:53.330
Oh? Didn't you say I could do what I wanted?

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.830
I did say you could do what you wanted.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:02.160
However, I will <i>not</i> allow you to do anything
that will degrade the dignity of Ayanagi...

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.120
...as the Hiragi family heir.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.040
This is pointless.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:17.700
I pray that your students will not be
eliminated at the upcoming test performance.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:23.700
It would set a bad example for a Star Team
to be eliminated before even six months pass.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.540
Well, just watch.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:31.500
I'll raise them to be musical
stars you've never seen before.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:37.330
You do not understand anything, do you, Otori?

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.290
It's not that I don't understand...

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:46.580
It's just that I don't
<i>want</i> to understand, Hiragi.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.620
When I think about the
play earlier, I lose my appetite.

00:18:57.620 --> 00:19:01.870
Why? Your tearful acting was really amazing!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.790
You think so? I could get used to hearing that.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:08.660
On the other hand, I couldn't do anything.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.660
I have to work harder.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:14.500
I'm jealous.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:18.040
It's amazing to be able to
always work hard and stay positive.

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:21.330
It's because I have someone who is my goal.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.200
Your goal?

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.410
Yeah.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:31.450
I applied for Ayanagi Academy
because I wanted to be like him.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:35.410
I hope you get to stand on
the same stage as him someday.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:42.000
I see... I might be able to stand on the
same stage as him if I continue on this path.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:45.660
In order to do that, I need to
catch up to everyone on the team first!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.160
I can't cause my friends trouble, either.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.450
Friends?

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:52.700
It might be a little early
to call you all friends, huh?

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:55.160
Hoshitani...

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.200
I'm going to do special
training starting tomorrow!

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.290
I'll do the special training with you.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:00.790
Really?

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:04.410
But I have just one favor to ask.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:06.700
I want you to take back what you said.

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:08.000
Because I

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.450
am already

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.330
your friend!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:29.500
♪ Before I knew it, I had
gotten a push from behind ♪

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:34.330
♪ And I wasn't just a coward anymore ♪

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:43.370
♪ When I was depressed,
your optimism saved me ♪

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:48.750
♪ No matter how small
the problem, I want to help ♪

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:55.450
♪ Because you're already my precious friend ♪

00:20:55.450 --> 00:21:01.200
♪ Can someone unreliable like
me be of any support to you? ♪

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:08.660
♪ Just smiling by your side ♪

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:14.250
♪ Like the sunlight on a clear morning ♪

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.910
♪ It reaches deep into the heart ♪

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:21.000
♪ A direct, dazzling brilliance ♪

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:28.700
♪ Even when times are hard,
I'll be your strength if you'll have me ♪

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:33.540
♪ 'Cause you're my friend... ♪

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:41.160
Nayuki... Thanks.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:50.000
These guys might be able to change...

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:54.120
...this tedious estate.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:58.000
Will betting on this guy pay off...

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.080
...or not?

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:25.870
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:32.370
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:35.870
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:40.160
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:44.290
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:47.540
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:51.120
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:55.080
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:58.250
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.120
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:05.620
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:09.410
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:12.950
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:16.620
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:22.620
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:36.580
Well, what is it?

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:38.120
Get rid of him.

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:40.250
You could tell with the improv, right?

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:43.000
At this point, he's way below the rest of us.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:48.870
We would have a better chance of surviving
if we got rid of him to form a four-person group.

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:58.370
"Act 3"

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:01.120
Tengenji, why are you so popular?

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.370
It's because I'm super cool.

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:04.700
Why are you so cool?

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:06.500
It's because I'm a genius.

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:08.000
Why are you such a genius?

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:11.790
That's because I am the great Kakeru Tengenji!

00:24:12.370 --> 00:24:19.950
"Support us next week, too."
